the closure types, the difference lookup-order.nocl records: cl names a closure `<lambda_<hash>>` at namespace scope where cxx1 writes `$_N` inside the function that made it, as clang does, so the four call operators differ by spelling alone; and cl emits a constructor for each closure taking its capture (`this`, an `int`), where cxx1 builds a closure in place and has no constructor to name. Every name this case is about - `S::k`, `S::twice`, `S::In`'s constructor - agrees, and what it measures is that the class's static, enumerator, typedef and nested class are in scope in the lambda, which run.sh checks on every target.
